### Training Checkpoint Recovery - raw HTTP request samples
### Usable directly in REST clients (VS Code REST Client, IntelliJ HTTP Client).
### Start the server: python -m checkpoint_service serve --port 8080

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8080
@run = rest-sample

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Create run (body optional; defaults shown explicitly)
POST {{base}}/runs/{{run}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "n_samples": 512,
  "n_features": 8,
  "data_seed": 20260925,
  "train_seed": 42,
  "batch_size": 32,
  "lr": 0.05,
  "momentum": 0.9,
  "l2": 0.0001,
  "n_epochs": 4,
  "checkpoint_every": 8
}

### Train up to 5 batches (a graceful pause; progress is committed)
POST {{base}}/runs/{{run}}/train
Content-Type: application/json

{"stop_after": 5}

### Status (e.g. after restarting the server process)
GET {{base}}/runs/{{run}}/status

### Resume and run until finished
POST {{base}}/runs/{{run}}/train
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Inspect checkpoint sections (model / optimizer / rng / cursor)
GET {{base}}/runs/{{run}}/checkpoint

### List runs
GET {{base}}/runs

### Error: duplicate run -> 409 RunExistsError
POST {{base}}/runs/{{run}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Error: corrupt checkpoint -> 422 CheckpointCorruptError
### (flip a byte in runs/<run>/checkpoint.payload first)
GET {{base}}/runs/{{run}}/status
